---
// Developer Kaki segment review: the review itself. A lead statement, then the account in two columns.
// Source for every claim: .source/content.md, "Case study: Developer Kaki"; the quoted description is
// Daren Tan's own, from LinkedIn (page note 5).
---

<section class="review" aria-labelledby="review-heading">
  <h2 id="review-heading" class="section-heading">Review</h2>

  <div class="body">
    <p class="lead" data-reveal>
      Developer Kaki is Malaysia’s largest developer community, and the bridge between local tech talent
      and the companies hiring it across Southeast Asia.
    </p>

    <div class="text" data-reveal>
      <p>
        Daren Tan founded the community as a Facebook group in February 2019. It is still anchored there,
        and has spread to LinkedIn, WhatsApp, XiaoHongShu and in-person events. Across them it counts more
        than <span class="tabular">72,000</span> members.<a class="note-ref" href="#note-1" aria-label="Note 1">1</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Its value is the signal it carries. Curated job postings have surfaced more than{' '}
        <span class="tabular">5,000</span> roles,<a class="note-ref" href="#note-2" aria-label="Note 2">2</a>{' '}
        and alongside them members share what they earn, what employers are like to work for and how their
        careers have moved. Daren describes it as “the most candid tech career signal in
        Malaysia”.<a class="note-ref" href="#note-5" aria-label="Note 5">5</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        The jobs have since outgrown the group. JOBS by Developer Kaki, a web portal operated under an
        employment-agency licence, has <span class="tabular">5,000</span> registered
        users,<a class="note-ref" href="#note-3" aria-label="Note 3">3</a>{' '}
        and <span class="tabular">MYR 50.5k</span> in payments was verified through its Payex-Xendit gateway
        between <span class="tabular">2023</span> and <span class="tabular">2026</span>.<a class="note-ref" href="#note-4" aria-label="Note 4">4</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

